# Optional self-host overrides. Leave these unset to generate unique values
# on first boot. They are stored in the selfhost_secrets Docker volume and
# reused after `docker compose down` (without -v).
#
# Copying this file to .env is optional. It does not contain usable keys.
#
#   docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.selfhost.yml up --build
#
# To choose values yourself, set all four before the first boot (export them
# or uncomment them here and copy this file to .env). Generate a set with:
#
#   node ops/selfhost/ensure-secrets.mjs --print
#
# SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET must be at least 32 characters. Sign both keys with
# that secret, HS256, with claim role "anon" or "service_role". See
# docs/self-host-reference.md.
#
# SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# SELFHOST_DB_PASSWORD=
#
# Published host ports. Default is loopback. A non-local bind refuses the
# old public placeholder keys.
#
# SELFHOST_BIND=127.0.0.1
